WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.140
- Okay, so I mean, Quaid
might be your last name,

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.200
but you also go by another
name, what is that?

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.090
I hear you have a nickname.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.811
- Oh yes, my friends refer
to me as Pool Noodle.

00:00:10.811 --> 00:00:12.620
(laughing)
- No!

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.850
- You've seen them in pools.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:14.860
- Yeah.
- They're just those like,

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.766
giant macaroni-looking
things that you float on.

00:00:17.766 --> 00:00:19.317
- (laughs) How tall are you?

00:00:19.317 --> 00:00:21.870
- It's just kind of the shape of my body

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.880
and the fact that I, you know,
I'm lanky and I'm noodle-y.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.510
And these are friends that have known me

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.950
since middle school, in which I was

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.450
way more uncoordinated.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.430
(laughing)
And it just seemed like I

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.960
had no bones, but I feel
like I should feel lucky

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.565
that my nickname is Pool
Noodle and not Inner Tube.

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:40.950
(laughing)
- Yeah, I was gonna say,

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.110
you just took my joke.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.790
I was like, I had another
one, mine was Inner Tube.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.230
No, literally, I would
love if people called me

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.626
a pool noodle.
- Pool noodle!

00:00:48.626 --> 00:00:51.250
- (laughs) I'd be like,
"I am feeling thin today."

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.210
No, that's awesome.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.400
So this summer though, your
girlfriend shared this photo.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.360
So, whose idea was this?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.193
- Oh!
(laughing)

00:00:58.193 --> 00:00:59.240
- [Kelly] 'Cause it's awesome.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.200
- It's Liz's, that was Liz's.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:06.980
She has this talent for kind
of finding really random,

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.380
insane, amazing experiences in new cities.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.910
This is in Toronto.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.457
I had no idea I was going
and basically, she was like,

00:01:14.457 --> 00:01:17.020
"Come with me, we're
gonna do something fun."

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.880
I'm like, "All right."

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.410
And we wound up going
to the YMCA in Toronto

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.370
and there were all these
people with mermaid tails.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.560
It was a mermaid class.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.560
This is a thing you can do.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.180
It's an entire culture, apparently.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.460
They refer to themselves as merfolk.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.423
(laughing)
They have Mercons.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.310
And I took the class and you
know, I put on a monofin.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.218
I know all the terminology now.

00:01:41.218 --> 00:01:43.018
(laughing)
- You're a merman, okay.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.413
This is so funny.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.220
- Oh my God.
- My four year old boy

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.580
is literally obsessed.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.600
He wants to be a merman.
- Aw!

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.090
- He's obsessed, 'cause
I think they were on,

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.520
Aquaman was on here?
- Oh, yeah.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.840
- And so from that moment,
he's all into like, yeah.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.590
- That actually sounds
up my alley, weirdly.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.063
I'd be into the mermaid
thing, I think that's so cool.

00:02:04.063 --> 00:02:06.600
- And you're the greatest boyfriend ever.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.940
You just showed up at something.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.177
You had no idea and you were like,

00:02:09.177 --> 00:02:13.750
"I guess I'll be a merman,"
like what boyfriend does that?

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.400
- Also, I don't want to brag,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.412
but I'm kind of great at being a mermaid.

00:02:18.412 --> 00:02:21.700
(laughing)
I took to it really quickly.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.340
Like, I'm to the point where,

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.990
when we shot season two of "The Boys,"

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.750
the next year, we did it
again at a different YMCA.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.610
And that was, right after the class,

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.650
it was my first time getting
recognized for the show.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.550
- Oh!
- Oh my gosh, I love you!

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.207
- So there was a guy that
came up and he was like,

00:02:38.207 --> 00:02:40.890
"Oh, I saw you um, doing your thing,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.830
but I didn't want to interrupt,
but I love the show."

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.120
So I'm like, "Okay, of course, yeah.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.730
The first time I get
recognized for the show,

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.930
I'm wearing a skirt, a mermaid skirt."

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.300
- A tail, that's amazing.
(laughing)

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.280
I love you so much,

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.130
that you're down for stuff like that.

